 "note": "The sedesert kit's adapter onto the material library (core/materials/PLAN.md). Keys are the kit's MAT slots (50-*-species.js; BIO.libSwap names an array entry by index, a nested table's entry as key.name). Grey detail maps (keep 0) normalised to the measured mean of the procedural map each replaces (2026-10-06), so the species tints keep their tone; prism gum keeps its own colour. Slots not listed stay procedural. Hosts that vendor the kit get these by inlining the kit's pack (tools/textures/matlib_pack.py). Run python3 tools/textures/pack.py biomes/sedesert after any change, then python3 build.py. lichen stays procedural: the kit draws it as small flat patches, and the nine-lichen card read as a gridded square on them. Slots drawn as a single plant (grass, reeds, fronds, palms, rosettes, paddles, moss) show one cell of their nine-plant sheet (`cell`, the middle one); crown and canopy cards keep the whole sheet. bloom (2026-10-06, late): card.flower.bloom, grey at the procedural map's mean, so each species' instance colour colours its flowers. groundDetail and groundCrack (2026-10-06, late): the host's ground layers multiplied over the painted ground (45-host-stage.js hostGroundLib), grey and bright (mean .9; cracks .95 with contrast 1.8), colour map only. The host's girder tower (2026-10-06, late; 85-host-tower.js hostTowerLib): concrete.ancient and metal.rust.plate at the procedural maps' brightness and colour, worked out from their painters. (2026-10-06, late) pods: card.pods, one cell (the hanging bean pods). column (2026-10-25): the giant candelabra's and the cardon's crown columns (M.column, 50-species) take skin.cactus, the trunks' own skin (the columns gained uv: once round, up the height).",
